# TODO - Android and browser packaging

## Objective

Support Android ARM64 and browser targets where compatible.

## Acceptance

- Use official Android and WASM toolchains on supported hosts.
- Test touch, storage, graphics capabilities and packaging.
- Report unavailable targets rather than claiming support.

## Evidence

Pending. Record actual checks and remaining limitations before completion.

Install the official Rust standard-library targets for the selected stable
toolchain. Cross-target library checks are mandatory in the shared
validator:

```sh
rustup target add aarch64-linux-android wasm32-unknown-unknown \
  aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu \
  aarch64-pc-windows-gnullvm x86_64-pc-windows-gnu
cargo validate --no-cache
```

This checks every workspace library under crates without default features.
New title packages enter the matrix automatically. The validation cache
includes the installed target inventory. It does not link an Android
application, produce a browser module, or execute either target.

