The native title now executes its existing interactive loop as a sequence
of bounded steps. Each step drains at most one admitted event batch,
advances the same fixed-step simulation, updates preferences and audio,
and submits at most one frame. The last static presentation survives
between calls, quit remains terminal, and the caller selects the event
wait. Native idle waiting and uncapped gameplay remain unchanged.
This is a preparation for callback-driven hosts, not an asynchronous
scene lifetime or a browser runtime.

